              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to create a friendly atmosphere and lead into the school-playground topic.\n*Procedure:\n- Greet the class and use a quick “Look and touch” game with a real book and a ball.\n- Show a school-playground picture and ask pupils to look for familiar objects.\n- Say: “Open your book. Unit 1 – In the school playground.”\n2. Presentation (12’)\nActivity 1. Listen and repeat.\n*Aims: pupils recognize B, b /b/ and repeat the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to the letter B, b and the four target items: book, ball, Bill, bike.\n- Play the official audio once. Pupils point to the pictures.\n- Play again, pausing after each item for choral repetition.\n- Model the /b/ sound clearly; ask pupils to watch the mouth and repeat.\n- Use realia/pictures to check meaning without lengthy translation.\n- Invite a few pupils to repeat individually; praise effort rather than speed.\n3. Practice (10’)\nActivity 2. Point and say.\n*Aims: pupils identify and say the target words with picture support.\n*Procedure:\n- Model: point to one picture and say the word.\n- Pupils practise as a whole class, then in pairs.\n- Play “Point fast”: T says a word; pupils point to the correct picture.\n- Change roles: T points; pupils say the word.\nDigital & AI mini-task: “AI says – Check the picture!”\n - T shows 3 teacher-prepared picture labels/voice examples. One AI-style example is deliberately wrong, e.g. a picture of a book labelled “ball”.\n - Ask pupils: “Right or wrong?” Pupils point to the textbook picture and say the correct word.\n - Re-play the official textbook audio to confirm. Emphasise: “Check first. AI can be wrong.”\n - Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies one wrong AI-style label and gives/points to the correct word.\n4. Production (6’)\n- Put picture cards around the board/classroom.\n- Say one word. Pupils point, mime or move a finger toward the correct card.\n- In pairs, one pupil points; the other says the word. Swap roles.\n- Give simple positive feedback.\n5. Homework / Wrap-up (3’)\n- Ask: “What letter today?” “What words?”\n- Pupils repeat B, b and 2–4 target words.\n- Ask pupils to point to B/b and target pictures in the book at home; no online task is required.",
