              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to review B, b and the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Show B/b cards and quickly review book, ball, Bill, bike.\n- Play a short “Show me” game: T says a word; pupils point to the matching picture.\n2. Practice (19’)\nActivity 3. Listen and chant.\n*Aims: pupils listen to and chant the target sound/words with rhythm.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw attention to the pictures and target letter.\n- Play the official chant once for listening only.\n- Play again; pupils point to the matching pictures.\n- Model the rhythm with claps/taps; pupils chant line by line.\n- Let groups chant; keep the pace comfortable for Grade 1 pupils.\nActivity 4. Listen and tick.\n*Aims: pupils identify the correct picture from the audio.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask pupils to look at the picture options before listening.\n- Play the official audio; pupils listen and tick.\n- Play again for checking.\n- Ask pupils to compare with a partner by pointing, not by reading long explanations.\n- Confirm answers with the class.\nActivity 5. Look and trace.\n*Aims: pupils recognize and trace B, b with correct direction.\n*Procedure:\n- Model B and b in the air and on the board.\n- Pupils finger-trace first, then trace in the book.\n- Monitor pencil grip and stroke direction.\n- Add a 20–30 second eye/hand rest after the screen/audio work.\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Label checker”\n - T displays three picture–word pairs from the lesson. One AI-style pair is wrong.\n - Pupils check with the textbook/realia and choose a simple symbol: ✓ or ✗ / thumbs up or down.\n - T asks selected pupils to point to the correct picture/word and replays official audio for confirmation.\n - Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one wrong picture label and explains by pointing/saying one word.\n3. Production (8’)\n- Play “B basket”: pupils sort teacher-held cards into B/b target words vs. a few non-B distractor pictures orally/visually.\n- Let pupils say at least one target word when placing/pointing.\n- End with a very short class chant/repetition.\n4. Wrap-up & Homework (4’)\n- Review: B, b; book, ball, Bill, bike.\n- Ask pupils to trace B/b once more on paper/air and say one word.\n- Home practice: look at the book and repeat with an adult if possible; no AI or personal device use is required.",
