              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to create a friendly atmosphere, review familiar language and lead into the new unit/lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Greet the class and use a quick picture/realia game.\n- Show the lesson context: In the dining room. Ask pupils to look, point or guess familiar items.\n- Say: “Open your book. Unit 2 – In the dining room.”\n\n2. Presentation (12’)\nActivity 1. Listen and repeat.\n*Aims: pupils recognize C, c and the target sound /k/, and repeat the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw pupils’ attention to C, c and the target words: cake, car, cat, cup.\n- Play the official audio once. Pupils listen and point.\n- Play again, pausing after each word for choral repetition.\n- Model the target sound /k/ clearly and let pupils repeat.\n- Use pictures/realia to check meaning.\n- Invite selected pupils to repeat individually; give encouraging feedback.\n\n3. Practice (10’)\nActivity 2. Point and say.\n*Aims: pupils identify and say target words with picture support.\n*Procedure:\n- Model: point to one picture and say the word.\n- Pupils practise as a class, then in pairs.\n- Play “Point fast”: T says a word; pupils point to the correct picture.\n- Reverse: T points; pupils say the word.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “C/c picture–voice check”\n - Teacher shows four C/c picture/voice examples with one deliberate mismatch. Pupils point to the correct picture and check with official audio.\n - Ask pupils to show Right/Wrong, ✓/✗ or point to the correct picture.\n - Confirm with the official textbook/audio. Remind pupils: “Check first. AI can be wrong.”\n - Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies/corrects one mismatch. Codes: AI 4.A2; NLS 1.1.CB1a.\n\n4. Production (6’)\n- Use picture cards/realia for a short pointing, matching or movement game.\n- In pairs, one pupil points; the other says the word. Swap roles.\n- Praise effort, clear listening and safe turn-taking.\n\n5. Wrap-up & Homework (3’)\n- Review C, c, /k/ and the target words.\n- Pupils point to and say 2–4 words.\n- Home practice: look at the book and repeat; no online/AI task is required.",
