              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to review I, i, /ɪ/ and the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Use picture cards for a quick point-and-say game.\n- Review: fish, chips, milk, chicken.\n\n2. Practice (18’)\nActivity 6. Listen and repeat.\n*Aims: pupils listen to and repeat the target sentence pattern in context.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask pupils to look at the pictures and identify familiar items/characters.\n- Play the official audio once for meaning.\n- Play again line by line for choral repetition.\n- Model the target language: I like fish/chips/milk/chicken.\n- Let pupils repeat in groups and individually.\n\nActivity 7. Let’s talk.\n*Aims: pupils use the target pattern with picture support.\n*Procedure:\n- Model one short exchange/sentence.\n- Pupils practise with textbook or teacher-prepared picture cards.\n- Pair work: point, say, listen and swap roles.\n\nActivity 8. Let’s sing.\n*Aims: pupils consolidate the target language through a simple song and actions.\n*Procedure:\n- Play the official song once.\n- Teach simple safe actions.\n- Sing line by line, then as a class/groups.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “I like… – choice stays with me”\n - Teacher shows generic food icons and an AI-style preference sentence. Pupils decide their own model response; AI does not decide a pupil’s preference.\n - AI/voice output is only a practice example; official audio and teacher feedback remain the checking sources.\n - Do not require pupils to record/upload their voices, faces, home or family information.\n - Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects/chooses one safe, accurate model. Codes: AI 4.A2; NLS 2.1.CB1a; NLS 4.2.CB1b.\n\n3. Production (8’)\n- Pupils use the model “I like fish/chips/milk/chicken.” with a picture card.\n- Invite volunteers/pairs to perform briefly.\n- Give supportive feedback; do not rank pupils by AI pronunciation scores.\n\n4. Wrap-up & Homework (5’)\n- Ask pupils to recall one word and one sentence pattern.\n- Review one digital-safety/checking rule: “Check with the book/audio.”\n- Home practice: sing/repeat from the book if possible; no AI account or upload is required.",
              "- Ss review familiar words and pictures.\n\n- Ss look at the lesson pictures.\n- Ss listen for meaning and repeat line by line.\n- Ss practise the target sentence pattern.\n\n- Ss point, speak and listen in pairs.\n- Ss swap roles.\n\n- Ss listen to the song.\n- Ss sing with simple safe actions.\n\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n - Ss compare one AI-style model with the official lesson evidence.\n - Ss correct/choose a safe and accurate model.\n - Ss do not upload voices, faces or private information.\n\n- Ss use the target pattern with picture cards.\n- Selected Ss/pairs perform.\n\n- Ss recall one word and one sentence.\n- Ss repeat the rule: check AI with book/audio."
