              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to review G, g and the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Show G, g and picture cards for girl, garden, goat, gate.\n- Play a quick “Show me / Point to” review game.\n\n2. Practice (20’)\nActivity 3. Listen and chant.\n*Aims: pupils listen to and chant the target sound/words with suitable rhythm.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw attention to the pictures and target letter.\n- Play the official chant once for listening only.\n- Play again; pupils point to the matching pictures.\n- Model the rhythm with claps/taps; pupils chant line by line and then in groups.\n\nActivity 4. Listen and tick.\n*Aims: pupils identify the correct pictures from official audio.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask pupils to look at picture options before listening.\n- Play the official audio; pupils listen and tick.\n- Play again for checking.\n- Let pupils compare by pointing, then confirm answers together.\n\nActivity 5. Look and trace G, g.\n*Aims: pupils recognize and trace G, g with correct direction.\n*Procedure:\n- Model G, g in the air and on the board.\n- Pupils finger-trace first, then trace in the book.\n- Monitor pencil grip and stroke direction.\n- Give a short eye/hand rest after screen/audio work.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Goat or gate? – listen and check”\n - Teacher presents an AI-style answer that confuses goat/gate or girl/garden. Pupils listen again, check G/g and the picture, then correct it.\n - Pupils use textbook picture/audio evidence before changing an answer.\n - Keep screen interaction brief; return to paper, speaking and movement.\n - Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one AI-style answer or label. Codes: AI 4.B2; NLS 1.2.CB1a.\n\n3. Production (7’)\n- Play a short letter/sound sorting or picture-matching game.\n- Invite pupils to say at least one target word.\n- Finish with one short class chant/repetition.\n\n4. Wrap-up & Homework (4’)\n- Review G, g and the target words.\n- Ask pupils to trace G, g once more in the air/paper.\n- Home practice is book-based; no personal-device use is required.",
              "- Ss review familiar words and pictures.\n\n- Ss look at the lesson pictures.\n- Ss listen for meaning and repeat line by line.\n- Ss practise the target sentence pattern.\n\n- Ss point, speak and listen in pairs.\n- Ss swap roles.\n\n- Ss listen to the song.\n- Ss sing with simple safe actions.\n\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n - Ss compare one AI-style model with the official lesson evidence.\n - Ss correct/choose a safe and accurate model.\n - Ss do not upload voices, faces or private information.\n\n- Ss use the target pattern with picture cards.\n- Selected Ss/pairs perform.\n\n- Ss recall one word and one sentence.\n- Ss repeat the rule: check AI with book/audio."
