              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to create a friendly atmosphere, review familiar language and lead into the new lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Greet the class and run a quick picture/realia review.\n- Introduce Unit 9: In the shop.\n- Ask pupils to observe the main picture and identify familiar people/objects.\n\n2. Presentation (12’)\nActivity 1. Listen and repeat.\n*Aims: pupils recognize O, o, pronounce /ɒ/ and repeat the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Draw attention to O, o and the words: locks, clocks, mops, pots.\n- Play the official audio once; pupils listen and point.\n- Play again, pausing for choral repetition.\n- Model /ɒ/ clearly; pupils repeat in class/groups/individually.\n- Use pictures/realia to check meaning.\n\n3. Practice (10’)\nActivity 2. Point and say.\n*Aims: pupils identify and say target words with picture support.\n*Procedure:\n- Model one item: point and say.\n- Pupils practise as a class and then in pairs.\n- Play a quick “Point fast / Say fast” game.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Shop object picture–voice check”\n- Teacher displays locks/clocks/mops/pots with one wrong AI-style label. Pupils point, say and verify using the textbook and official audio.\n- Pupils show ✓/✗, Right/Wrong or point to the corrected item.\n- Confirm with the official textbook/audio. Reinforce: “AI can be wrong. Check first.”\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil identifies/corrects one mismatch. Codes: AI 4.A2; NLS 1.1.CB1a.\n\n4. Production (6’)\n- Use picture cards/realia for a short matching, pointing or movement game.\n- In pairs: one pupil points; the other says the word. Swap roles.\n\n5. Wrap-up & Homework (3’)\n- Review O, o, /ɒ/ and the target words.\n- Pupils say 2–4 words from memory or picture cues.\n- Home practice: repeat from the book; no AI account or upload is required.",
