              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to review O, o and the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Display O, o and picture cards for locks, clocks, mops, pots.\n- Run a quick “Show me / Point to” game.\n\n2. Practice (20’)\nActivity 3. Listen and chant.\n*Aims: pupils listen and chant the target sound/words with suitable rhythm.\n*Procedure:\n- Let pupils observe the pictures and target letter.\n- Play the official chant once for listening.\n- Play again; pupils point and clap/tap the rhythm.\n- Chant line by line, then in groups.\n\nActivity 4. Listen and tick.\n*Aims: pupils identify the correct pictures from official audio.\n*Procedure:\n- Pupils look at picture options before listening.\n- Play the official audio; pupils listen and tick.\n- Play again for checking; compare by pointing.\n\nActivity 5. Look and trace/write O, o.\n*Aims: pupils recognize and form O, o correctly.\n*Procedure:\n- Model O, o in the air and on the board.\n- Pupils finger-trace first, then trace/write in the book.\n- Monitor pencil grip and stroke direction.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “Count it yourself”\n- Teacher shows an AI-style count for a group of 2–5 shop objects, including one wrong count. Pupils point to each object, count themselves and correct the answer.\n- Pupils use picture/audio evidence before changing an answer.\n- Keep screen interaction brief and return to paper, speech and movement.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects one AI-style answer/label/count. Codes: AI 4.B2; NLS 1.2.CB1a.\n\n3. Production (7’)\n- Play a short letter/sound sorting or picture-matching game.\n- Invite pupils to say at least one target word.\n\n4. Wrap-up & Homework (4’)\n- Review O, o and the target words.\n- Air-write O, o once more.\n- Home practice is book/paper based; personal-device use is not required.",
