              "1. Warm-up (4’)\n*Aims: to review M, m, /m/ and the target words.\n*Procedure:\n- Use picture cards for a quick point-and-say review.\n- Review: mango, mother, mouse, monkey.\n\n2. Practice (18’)\nActivity 6. Listen and repeat.\n*Aims: pupils listen to and repeat the target sentence pattern in context.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask pupils to observe the lesson pictures.\n- Play official audio once for meaning and again line by line.\n- Model: That’s a monkey/mouse/mango. / That’s my mother.\n- Practise chorally, in groups and individually.\n\nActivity 7. Let’s talk.\n*Aims: pupils use the target pattern with picture support.\n*Procedure:\n- Model one short exchange/sentence.\n- Pupils practise with textbook or teacher-prepared picture cards.\n- Pair work: point, say, listen and swap roles.\n\nActivity 8. Let’s sing.\n*Aims: pupils consolidate the target language through a simple song and safe actions.\n*Procedure:\n- Play the official song once.\n- Teach simple safe actions; sing line by line, then together.\n\nDigital & AI mini-task: “That’s a… – picture caption check”\n- Teacher displays a generic zoo/family scene with one incorrect AI-style caption. Pupils point and produce the correct “That’s …” sentence.\n- AI/voice output is only a practice example; official audio and teacher feedback remain the checking references.\n- Pupils are not required to record/upload their voices, faces, home, family, health or location information.\n- Digital/AI evidence: pupil corrects/chooses one safe, accurate model. Codes: AI 4.A2; NLS 2.1.CB1a; NLS 4.2.CB1b.\n\n3. Production (8’)\n- Pupils use the model “That’s a monkey/mouse/mango. / That’s my mother.” with a picture card.\n- Invite volunteers/pairs to perform briefly.\n- Give supportive feedback; do not rank pupils using AI-generated scores.\n\n4. Wrap-up & Homework (5’)\n- Ask pupils to recall one word and one sentence pattern.\n- Review the rule: “Check AI with the book/audio/teacher.”\n- Home practice: repeat/sing from the book; no AI account or upload is required.",
              "- Ss review familiar words and pictures.\n\n- Ss observe the lesson pictures.\n- Ss listen for meaning and repeat line by line.\n- Ss practise the sentence pattern.\n\n- Ss point, speak and listen in pairs.\n- Ss swap roles.\n\n- Ss listen to the song.\n- Ss sing with simple safe actions.\n\nDigital/AI pupil actions:\n- Ss compare one AI-style model with official lesson evidence.\n- Ss correct/choose a safe and accurate model.\n- Ss avoid sharing private information or uploading personal media.\n\n- Ss use the target pattern with picture cards.\n- Selected Ss/pairs perform.\n\n- Ss recall one word and one sentence.\n- Ss repeat the checking/safety rule."
